(7701300, 1263702, 1031, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by GolferDDS:</b></div><hr/><i> Not an easy shot too get. Everything has to be just right and timing is essential. Great capture. Congrats on the yellow. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Indeed! And it makes me wonder if this would have grabbed the red with a tighter/square crop ...</td>', 'Originally posted by GolferDDS: Not an easy shot too get. Everything has to be just right and timing is essential. Great capture. Congrats on the yellow.  Indeed! And it makes me wonder if this would have grabbed the red with a tighter/square crop ...', '2021-09-14 18:48:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(7701425, 1263643, 49520, '<td valign="top">Unfortunately, access further in front of the spider was impossible due to a brick wall in the way. That would certainly have been a wonderful shot. On the other hand, you do see the thick mandibles plunged into the abdomen of the wasp from this angle.<br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by willem:</b></div><hr/><i> I would have liked to see the head/jaws of the spider, to match the title of the image. </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'Unfortunately, access further in front of the spider was impossible due to a brick wall in the way. That would certainly have been a wonderful shot. On the other hand, you do see the thick mandibles plunged into the abdomen of the wasp from this angle.Originally posted by willem: I would have liked to see the head/jaws of the spider, to match the title of the image. ', '2021-09-15 17:50:01.000000', NULL, 0),
